consuming. A pragmatic approach: create a small set of true components (Header, Footer, FeatureStrip, ProductCard, ProductCardHover, PageBanner, BlogPostCard, etc.) and use instances across the 9 frames. That satisfies \"component reuse\" evaluation.\n\nLayout plan (1440 wide frames):\n\n**Design system:**\n- Brand: #B88E2F\n- Neutrals: \n  - Background: #FFFFFF\n  - Light tint: #F9F1E7 (cream, common in Furniro kit) for hero background and section tints\n  - Soft gray: #F4F5F7 (product card photo bg)\n  - Text primary: #3A3A3A\n  - Text secondary: #898989\n  - Dark: #1A1A1F (footer bg is dark #000000 in original; but I can define my own — the original Furniro footer is dark #000000 with white text)\n  - Border: #E8E8E8 / #D6D6D6\n- Sale badge: #E97132 (original), New badge: #2EC1AC (original). I can define my own: Sale #E4572E, New #2EC1AC.\n- Rating star: #FFC700 (given, may change)\n- Type scale (Poppins):\n  - Display/Hero: 48-64 Bold\n  - H1 section: 32-40 Semibold\n  - H2: 28 Semibold\n  - H3 card title: 20 Medium/Semibold\n  - Body: 16 Regular\n  - Small: 14 Regular\n  - Caption/price: 20 Semibold (price), old price 16 Regular strikethrough #B0B0B0\n- Spacing: 8pt grid; container 1320 (60 margins) or 1360 (40 margins). I'll use 64px side margins (content width 1312) matching the brief page.\n\n**Frame heights** (free, every page scrolls):\n1. 01_Home: ~3600px tall\n2. 02_Shop: ~3400px\n3. 03_Product: ~2900px\n4. 04_Cart_Drawer: ~product page height with drawer overlay\n5. 05_Comparison: ~3300px (comparison table is long)\n6. 06_Cart: ~1700px\n7. 07_Checkout: ~2200px\n8. 08_Contact: ~1900px\n9. 09_Blog: ~2200px\n\nLayout of frames on workspace page: place in 2 columns, 1440 wide each with gaps. Positions: x=0 and x=1600, rows spaced by height. I'll compute as I build.\n\n**Build order:**\n1. Create master components section (x offset to the right, e.g., x=3400+): Header, Footer, FeatureStrip, ProductCard, ProductCardHover, PageBanner, Pagination? (Maybe simpler inline), BlogPostCard, etc.\n2. Build 01_Home\n3. Build 02_Shop\n4. Build 03_Product\n5. Build 04_Cart_Drawer\n6. Build 05_Comparison\n7. Build 06_Cart\n8. Build 07_Checkout\n9. Build 08_Contact\n10. Build 09_Blog\n11. Prototype links on all frames\n12. Screenshots + fixes\n\nGiven the 50k char limit per use_figma call and complexity, I'll write helper functions in each call. Each call needs to re-define helpers since state doesn't persist between calls. Actually, does the plugin sandbox persist state between use_figma calls? Not guaranteed. I'll keep each call self-contained with helpers re-defined.\n\nKey helper functions:\n- `solid(hex, opacity)` → paint\n- `txt(chars, size, style, hex, opts)` → text node (await figma.loadFontAsync for each style)\n- `mkFrame(name, w, h, fills)` → frame\n- `inst(compId)` → instance of component\n\nFonts to load: Poppins Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold. (Note: \"Semi Bold\" style name for Poppins! The gotcha says for Inter it's \"Semi Bold\" — for Poppins in Figma it's also \"SemiBold\"? Actually Poppins in Google Fonts has \"SemiBold\" as the style name in Figma. Let me check: The Figma gotcha note says Inter uses \"Semi Bold\". For Poppins, Figma lists styles: Thin, ExtraLight, Light, Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, ExtraBold, Black. Poppins style names in Figma are \"SemiBold\" (no space) I believe. Hmm, risky. Let me test by listing available fonts.\n\nI should run a quick script to check which Poppins styles are available.\n\nFor images: The photo components have image fills. When I create instances and resize them, the image fill scales (imagePaint scaleMode presumably CROP or FILL). Instances of components with image fills can be resized fine.\n\nFor icons: recoloring instances — icons are components with vector children with fills. I can override fills on instance children via `instance.findOne` and set fills. That works on instances (overridable).\n\nLet me plan the components I'll create in the workspace as masters (in a \"Components\" area at bottom of workspace page or a separate area):\n\n1. **Header** (1440×80): auto-layout horizontal, padding 40/64? Original Furniro header: logo left-ish, nav center, icons right. I'll do: frame 1440×80, padding H 54, logo group (Logo_Furniro 44×44 + \"Furniro\" 34 SemiBold bold-ish), nav centered (Home, Shop, About, Contact — 16 Medium), icons right (account, search, heart, cart 22-28px with 32 gap).\n   - For \"current\" nav state: I'll leave all nav items same color by default (#000) and override instance text color to brand for current. That's an instance override — allowed.\n\n2. **Footer** (1440×~380): dark bg #1A1A1A? Original: black bg. My choice: #24252B or #000. Original Furniro footer bg is #000000, text white, headings 24, links gray #EFEFEF... I'll do bg #1F1F24, 4 columns: Furniro. + address | Links | Help | Newsletter. Bottom: \"2023 Furniro. All rights reserved\" separated by top border.\n\n3. **FeatureStrip** (1440×~270): light bg #FAF4EE? Original: #F9F1E7-ish cream. 4 items: icon + title (SemiBold 20) + line (Regular 14, gray, possibly 2 lines).\n\n4. **PageBanner** (1440×~316): Photo_Page_Banner image stretched full width 1440×316 with CROP fill, overlay title (SemiBold 48) + breadcrumb (Home › X). Instance of Photo_Page_Banner resized to 1440×316.\n\n5. **ProductCard** (285×~420): auto-layout: photo area 285×301 (bg #F4F5F7, image fit), badge overlay (top-right), text area padding 24-28: name (SemiBold 24 #3A3A3A), desc (Medium 16 #898989), price row (SemiBold 20 #3A3A3A + old price Regular 16 #B0B0B0 strikethrough).\n   - Card width: 4-col grid on 1312 content: (1312 - 3*32)/4 = 304. Original uses 285 with 32 gaps. Content width 1312: 4×285 + 3×~24 = 1140+72 = 1212... Let me use 4 cols × 295 + 3×40 = 1180+120=1300 ≈ 1312 with 40 gaps: 4×298=1192 +120 = 1312. I'll use card width 295, gap 40, content 1300, margins 70. Fine — grid is mine to define. Actually let me standardize: content width 1280, margins 80. Card w 292, g