{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a full Figma product design benchmark: build the complete \"Furniro — furniture store website\" design (desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode) inside the \"03 · Workspace\" page (node 15:2) of the assigned Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG/ (fileKey `iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG`). Requirements from the task instructions and the user's Chinese-language message:\n   - Call whoami before writing and confirm account is zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE — confirmed; user_id 1692091428764723877; on \"Sensenova design\" enterprise plan with Full seat).\n   - Read \"00 · Start Here\" for product/screens/states/data/copy/prototype requirements; if app name disagrees, use the brief's product (Furniro).\n   - Read \"01 · Foundations\" for design rules (brand color #B88E2F and Poppins are FIXED; all other colors, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation, grid are mine to define and apply consistently).\n   - Reuse components in \"02 · Components\" (only default Button and default Text Field given) and assets in \"04 · Media\" (logo, photos, social logos, icons as components; icons neutral #1A1A1F recolorable; keep social logos unaltered).\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their existing nodes; keep existing unrelated content intact; do NOT create a different file or switch accounts.\n   - Build exactly 9 frames named exactly: 01_Home, 02_Shop, 03_Product, 04_Cart_Drawer, 05_Comparison, 06_Cart, 07_Checkout, 08_Contact, 09_Blog (one state per frame), wire them as a clickable prototype with listed links. Copy/data must match \"Fixed data\" exactly. Design header, footer, navigation and every business component as reusable components. Frame names are fixed; must-include lists state WHAT, not layout.\n   - Use live tool schemas; inspect screenshots of all screens; fix visible problems; finish screens, states and prototype flows before final answer.\n   - Final response must report: assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n   - Format requirement: before EVERY tool call include a concise visible decision summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:`; after each tool result do the same before the next call; final response starts with `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via `mcp__figma__use_figma` (JS code, 50k char limit per call; no persistent state between calls — helpers must be redefined each call)\n   - `figma.loadFontAsync` required before text creation; Poppins styles: \"SemiBold\" (NO space), \"Bold\", \"Medium\", \"Regular\"\n   - Media assets are COMPONENTS; create instances via `getNodeByIdAsync(id).createInstance()`; photo components have IMAGE fill with scaleMode \"FILL\" so resizing crops automatically\n   - `InstanceNode.swapComponent(componentNode)` works for swapping nested photo instances inside card instances (tested OK)\n   - Prototype wiring: `node.interactions` does NOT exist; `node.reactions` setter EXISTS but action schema failed on first attempt — error reveals valid action.type values: \"CONDITIONAL\" (needs conditionalBlocks), \"BACK\"|\"CLOSE\", \"URL\" (needs url), \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\" (needs mediaAction etc.), \"SET_VARIABLE\" (needs variableId), \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\" (needs variableCollectionId+variableModeId), plus one variant requiring a \"transition\" field — hypothesis: NODE navigation action requires `transition` to be provided (retry with `transition: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3}`)\n   - Component masters placed on the same Workspace page (allowed); instance