hoto_Recent_2 13:71, Photo_Recent_3 13:55, Photo_Recent_4 13:56, Photo_Recent_5 13:57. Icons: Icon_Account 13:33, Icon_Arrow_Right 13:49, Icon_Calendar 13:37, Icon_Cart 13:26, Icon_Cart_Close 13:39, Icon_Chevron_Down 13:30, Icon_Chevron_Right 13:46, Icon_Clock 13:54, Icon_Compare 13:47, Icon_Delete 13:28, Icon_Filter 13:50, Icon_Grid 13:48, Icon_Guarantee 13:42, Icon_Heart 13:53, Icon_Location 13:29, Icon_Phone 13:32, Icon_Remove 13:43, Icon_Search 13:40, Icon_Share 13:51, Icon_Shipping 13:25, Icon_Star 13:31 (yellow #FFC700), Icon_Star_Half 13:52, Icon_Support 13:41, Icon_Tag 13:27, Icon_Trophy 13:38, Icon_User 13:45, Icon_View_List 13:34.\n   - **Created so far on 03 · Workspace (15:2)**: Header COMPONENT id **19:4** (1440×88, white bg, padding L/R 54, SPACE_BETWEEN: LogoGroup=[Logo_Furniro inst 44×44 + \"Furniro\" Poppins SemiBold 30 #24252B], Nav gap 60 with texts named Nav_Home/Nav_Shop/Nav_About/Nav_Contact (Medium 16 #24252B), Actions gap 40 with Icon_Account/Icon_Search/Icon_Heart/Icon_Cart instances 24px) and Footer COMPONENT id **19:22** (height 478, bg #1F1F24, padding 64/60/36/60, gap 56; Columns row gap 110: Brand col [\"Furniro.\" Bold 26 white, address w280 Medium 16 #EFEFEF lh26 \"400 University Drive Suite 200, Coral Gables, FL 33134 USA\"], Links col (SemiBold 18 white + LinkList gap 18 with texts named Link_Home/Link_Shop/Link_About/Link_Contact/Link_Blog, Medium 16 #EFEFEF), Help col (Link_Payment Options/Link_Returns/Link_Privacy Policies), Newsletter col (email input 250×56 transparent w/ white 1px stroke + text \"Enter Your Email Address\" 13, SubscribeBtn 130×56 #B88E2F + \"SUBSCRIBE\" SemiBold 14 white); Divider 1320×1 #3A3A3A layoutAlign STRETCH; Copyright \"2023 Furniro. All rights reserved\" centered Medium 16 #EFEFEF). Footer description notes Blog link is entry to 09_Blog.\n   - **Helper functions pattern (redefine in EVERY use_figma call)**:\n```js\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s});\nfunction hex(h,o){const n=parseInt(h,16);return {type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o===undefined?1:o};}\nfunction txt(chars,style,size,colorHex,opts={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[hex(colorHex)];if(opts.ls!==undefined)t.letterSpacing={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:opts.ls};if(opts.lh)t.lineHeight={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:opts.lh};if(opts.deco)t.textDecoration=opts.deco;if(opts.w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(opts.w,t.height);}if(opts.align)t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align;return t;}\nfunction autolayout(name,dir,gap,pT,pR,pB,pL,parent){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.layoutMode=dir;f.itemSpacing=gap;f.paddingTop=pT;f.paddingRight=pR;f.paddingBottom=pB;f.paddingLeft=pL;f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.fills=[];if(parent)parent.appendChild(f);return f;}\nfunction frame(name,w,h,parent,x,y){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;if(w)f.resize(w,h);if(parent)parent.appendChild(f);if(x!==undefined)f.x=x;if(y!==undefined)f.y=y;return f;}\nasync function comp(id){return (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).createInstance();}\nasync function icon(id,size,colorHex,parent,name){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();i.resize(size,size*(c.height/c.width));i.name=name||c.name;if(colorHex){for(const d of i.findAll(n=>[\"VECTOR\",\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\",\"TEXT\",\"RECTANGLE\"].includes(n.type))){if(\"fills\" in d){try{d.fills=[hex(colorHex)];}catch(e){}}}}if(parent)parent.appendChild(i);return i;}\n```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`node.interactions` not supported**: `tmp.interactions = [...]` → \"no such property 'interactions' on FRAME node\". Pivoted to testing `node.reactions`.\n   - **`reactions` validation failure**: `{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"1:23\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\"}}` failed with detailed zod-style error. Valid action types per error: \"CONDITIONAL\" (requires conditionalBlocks), \"BACK\"|\"CLOSE\", \"URL\" (requires url), \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\" (requires mediaAction), \"SET_VARIABLE\" (requires variableId), \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\" (requires variableCollectionId+variableModeId), and one variant fragment requiring \"transition\" (\"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched: Required value missing at [0].action.transition\"). NEXT ATTEMPT: include `transition` in the NODE action, e.g. `action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"19:4\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3}}` — destinationId/navigation keys were flagged \"Unrecognized\" only within the tried variant contexts; the NODE variant likely requires transition.\n   - **ReferenceError: 'frame' is not defined** (first master-build call, died at Footer EmailInput line ~52): Header was fully created before the error; Footer was partial. Fixed by: in next call, deleting all nodes named \"Footer\" on the workspace page (`for (const ch of [...ws.children]) { if (ch.name === \"Footer\") ch.remove(); }`), reusing the existing Header (found via `ws.children.find(c => c.name === \"Header\" && c.type === \"COMPONENT\")`), defining the missing `frame()` helper, and rebuilding Footer completely. LESSON: verify every helper is defined before use; build calls must be self-contained.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed account + file structure; extracted complete brief and all fixed data/copy (preserved below); catalogued all media component IDs.\n   - Verified Poppins \"SemiBold\" style name, photo IMAGE fills crop on resize (scaleMode FILL), Text Field/Button internal structures for instance overrides.\n   - Established prototype-link strategy: reactions setter exists; must determine correct NODE action schema (retry with transition). If truly unsupported, must report limitation honestly.\n   - Product card image variation strategy: master ProductCard embeds one photo instance (Syltherine) named \"Photo\"; per-instance images changed via `swapComponent` (tested working).\n   - Planned workspace layout: two columns — x=0: 01_Home y=0, 03_Product y≈3800, 05_Comparison y≈7000, 07_Checkout y≈10600, 09_Blog y≈13200; x=1600: 02_Shop y=0, 04_Cart_Drawer y≈3800, 06_Cart y≈7000, 08_Contact y≈9500; masters section at x=3300 (Header y=0, Footer y=200; next masters below).\n   - 04_Cart_Drawer plan: clone finished 03_Product frame, shrink to ~1000 tall (content clipped), add dark scrim + 480px white right drawer with \"Shopping Cart\" header + Icon_Cart_Close, item row (Photo_Asgaard_Sofa, \"Asgaard sofa\", \"1 × Rs. 250,000.00\", Icon_Remove), Subtotal row, action buttons Cart/Checkout/Comparison.\n   - **Design system (my definitions)**: brand #B88E2F; cream #FBF1E7 (hero/section tint); creamDeep #F9F1E7 (feature strip, totals card, pagination inactive); card photo bg #F4F3EF; dark text #24252B; body #3A3A3A; gray #898989; light #B0B0B0; border #E5E5E5; input border #9F9F9F; sale badge #E97132; new badge #2EC1AC; footer bg #1F1F24; footer text #EFEFEF; star #FFC700. Type scale: hero 52 Bold; section title 40 SemiBold; page banner 48 SemiBold; card title 22 SemiBold; price 20 SemiBold; old price 16 Regular strikethrough; body 16; small 14; nav 16 Medium. Buttons: primary = #B88E2F bg white text (BUY NOW, Check Out, Place order, Submit, drawer Checkout, SUBSCRIBE); secondary = white bg, 1px #B88E2F border, #B88E2F text (Add To Cart on product, Show More, Explore More, drawer Cart, comparison Add To Cart); + Compare = white bg 1px dark border.\n   - **COMPLETE FIXED DATA (verbatim, must match)**:\n     - **Products (order)**: Syltherine · Stylish cafe chair · Rs. 2,500,000.00 · old Rs. 3,500,000.00 · badge -30% (13:21); Leviosa · Stylish cafe chair · Rs. 2,500,000.00 (13:17); Lolito · Luxury big sofa · Rs. 7,000,000.00 · old Rs. 14,000,000.00 · -50% (13:18); Respira · Outdoor bar table and stool · Rs. 500,000.00 · New (13:20); Grifo · Night lamp · Rs. 1,500,000.00 (13:73); Muggo · Small mug · Rs. 150,000.00 · New (13:19); Pingky · Cute bed set · Rs. 7,000,000.00 · old Rs. 14,000,000.00 · -50% (13:67); Potty · Minimalist flower pot · Rs. 500,000.00 · New (13:66).\n     - **Asgaard sofa (03)**: Rs. 250,000.00 · rating 4.7 · 204 Customer Reviews · Reviews [204]; Size L·XL·XS (selected L); Color purple #816DFA, black #000000, gold #B88E2F; SKU SS001; Category Sofas; Tags Sofa, Chair, Home, Shop. Short: \"Setting the bar as one of the most comfortable sofas in its class, the Asgaard is a compact, sturdy three-seater with a solid-wood frame and deep, soft cushions.\" Desc ¶1: \"Embodying the relaxed, honest spirit of Scandinavian design, the Asgaard pairs a solid-wood frame with soft, hard-wearing upholstery, built to be lived on every day.\" ¶2: \"Weighing in at 45 kg, the Asgaard is sturdy without being bulky. Its high-density foam cushions keep their shape, the removable covers are easy to care for, and the low, clean silhouette fits a small apartment as comfortably as a large living room.\"\n     - **Comparison (05)**: Asgaard Sofa · Rs. 250,000.00 · 4.7 · 204 Review (13:4) | Outdoor Sofa Set · Rs. 224,000.00 · 4.2 · 145 Review (13:14). General — Sales Package: 1 sectional sofa | 1 Three Seater, 2 Single Seater; Model Number: TFCBLIGRBL6SRHS | DTUBLIGRBL568; Secondary Material: Solid Wood | Solid Wood; Configuration: L-shaped | L-shaped; Upholstery Material: Fabric + Cotton | Fabric + Cotton; Upholstery Color: Bright Grey & Lion | Bright Grey & Lion. Product — Filling Material: Foam | Foam; Finish Type: Matte | Matte; Adjustable Headrest: No | Yes; Maximum Load Capacity: 280 KG | 300 KG; Origin of Manufacture: India | India. Dimensions — Width: 265.32 cm | 265.32 cm; Height: 76 cm | 76 cm; Depth: 167.76 cm | 167.76 cm; Weight: 45 KG | 65 KG; Seat Height: 41.52 cm | 41.52 cm; Leg Height: 5.46 cm | 5.46 cm. Warranty — Warranty Summary: 1 Year Manufacturing Warranty | 1.2 Year Manufacturing Warranty; Warranty Service Type: For Warranty Claims or Any Product Related Issues Please Email at operations@furniro.example | … at support@furniro.example; Covered in Warranty: Warranty Against Manufacturing Defect | Warranty of the product is limited to manufacturing defects only.; Not Covered in Warranty (both): The Warranty Does Not Cover Damages Due To Usage Of The Product Beyond Its Intended Use And Wear & Tear In The Natural Course Of Product Usage.; Domestic Warranty: 1 Year | 3 Months.\n     - **Features strip**: High Quality · crafted from top materials (Icon_Trophy 13:38); Warranty Protection · Over 2 years (Icon_Guarantee 13:42); Free Shipping · Order over Rs. 150,000 (Icon_Shipping 13:25); 24 / 7 Support · Dedicated support (Icon_Support 13:41). On frames 02 and 05–09 only (NOT 03).\n     - **Checkout (07)**: Country/Region Sri Lanka; Province Western Province; Direct Bank Transfer note: \"Make your payment directly into our bank account. Please use your Order ID as the payment reference. Your order will not be shipped until the funds have cleared in our account.\"; Privacy note: \"Your personal data will be used to support your experience throughout this website, to manage access to your account, and for other purposes described in our privacy policy.\" Order summary: headers Product | Subtotal; \"Asgaard sofa × 1\" Rs. 250,000.00; Subtotal Rs. 250,000.00; Total Rs. 250,000.00.\n     - **Contact (08)**: Intro \"For more information about our products & services, please feel free to drop us an email. Our staff will always be there to help you out. Do not hesitate!\"; Address \"236 5th SE Avenue, New York NY10000, United States\"; Phone \"Mobile: +(84) 546-6789 · Hotline: +(84) 456-6789\"; Working Time \"Monday–Friday: 9:00 – 22:00 · Saturday–Sunday: 9:00 – 21:00\"; form placeholders: Your name \"Abc\", Email address \"Abc@def.com\", Subject \"This is optional\", Message \"Hi! I'd like to ask about\"; button \"Submit\".\n     - **Blog (09)**: A