{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 6 masters built successfully (FS=20:4, PB=20:29, PC=20:39 h434, PH=20:50, PG=20:75, BP=20:84 h250).\n\nBut reactions still fail with both INSTANT and DISSOLVE. The error is truncated. Let me get the FULL error message this time to understand exactly which action types and fields are accepted. The previous full error from the summary listed: \"CONDITIONAL\" (requires conditionalBlocks), \"BACK\"|\"CLOSE\", \"URL\" (requires url), \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\" (needs mediaAction etc.), \"SET_VARIABLE\" (needs variableId), \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\" (needs variableCollectionId+variableModeId), plus one variant requiring a \"transition\" field.\n\nInteresting: the \"transition\" variant. When I passed type \"NODE\", it said invalid literal. So the transition-requiring variant must have a DIFFERENT type literal. What could it be? In newer Figma plugin API, there are action types for prototype: Actually in the modern PrototypeProtocol (used by Figma Slides/FigJam and newer design prototyping), actions include \"NAVIGATE\"? Hmm but the error said expected literals... The first attempt error listed: 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' for one branch. Let me just capture the FULL error text in the next call to see all accepted literals. I'll do a tiny call that sets reactions with a dummy and returns the complete error message.\n\nActually, let me think about what variants exist in this SDK version. The error mentioned a branch with \"transition\" required. In the Figma plugin typings for `Reaction`:\n\n```ts\ninterface Reaction {\n  readonly trigger: Trigger;\n  readonly action: Action;\n}\ntype Action =\n  ActionNavigate? \n```\n\nHmm, the standard plugin API Action types are:\n- `Action { type: \"BACK\" } | { type: \"CLOSE\" } | { type: \"URL\", url: string } | { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: string, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\"|\"OVERLAY\"|\"CHANGE_TO\"|\"SWAP\", transition: Transition, overlay?: ... } | { type: \"SET_VARIABLE\", variableId, ... } | { type: \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\", variableCollectionId, variableModeId } | { type: \"CONDITIONAL\", conditionalBlocks } | { type: \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\", ... }`\n\nSo the \"NODE\" action DOES exist in the real API and requires `transition`! The validation error said \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" for ONE branch, but the transition-requiring branch might accept \"NODE\". Wait — in my latest attempts I passed type \"NODE\" WITH transition and it still failed with \"Invalid literal value, expected 'CONDIT...\" — the error is truncated at the first branch's complaint (\"expected CONDITIONAL\"). The full error would list all branch issues. Since I can't see the full message (truncated to 200 chars), the NODE action might have failed in the transition branch for a different reason — e.g., the transition object shape is wrong, or navigation is required, or destinationId must reference a node in a DIFFERENT page? Hmm, destinationId \"19:4\" is the Header component on the same page. Maybe destination must be a FRAME, not a COMPONENT? That could be it! Prototype links navigate between FRAMES, and a component node might be an invalid destination. The validation might do a deeper semantic check... but zod schema errors are shape-only. Hmm.\n\nOr maybe the transition enum differs: valid types might be \"DISSOLVE\" | \"SMART_ANIMATE\" | \"MOVE_IN\" | \"MOVE_OUT\" | \"SLIDE_IN\" | \"SLIDE_OUT\" | \"SCROLL_ANIMATE\". \"INSTANT\" might not be valid, and DISSOLVE might need `easing` or duration constraints. But the error prefix is about ACTION not matching any oneOf — meaning every branch rejected. For the NODE branch, the rejection reason is hidden in the truncated part.\n\nBest move: run a call that returns the FULL error message (up to ~3000 chars) for the NODE+transition attempt, and also try variations:\n1. `{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:<a FRAME on the page>, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3}}` \n2. NODE with transition including easing\n3. Maybe action type \"NAVIGATE\"?\n\nI'll write a test harness that tries multiple shapes and returns each full error (truncated to 600 chars each). Let me create a temporary frame and a temporary destination FRAME (not component) on the workspace page.\n\nVariations to test:\nA: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:destFrame.id, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3}}\nB: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:destFrame.id, transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3}} (no navigation)\nC: {type:\"NAVIGATE\", destinationId:destFrame.id, transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3}}\nD: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:destFrame.id, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"INSTANT\",duration:0}}\nE: {type:\"NODE\", destinationId:destFrame.id, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\",duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"}}} — hmm easing shape? In plugin API, transition has `easing?: Easing`. Easing types: {type:\"EASE_IN\"|\"EASE_OUT\"|\"EASE_IN_OUT\"|\"LINEAR\"} or bezier {type:\"BEZIER\", ...}. Probably optional.\n\nReturn full errors for A and B at least (the most likely). To save tokens, capture e.message slice(0, 1200) for A, and for others just OK/FAIL+slice(0,300).\n\nLet me run this test now. Also clean up temp nodes after.","signature":"1cdeeec61c1c4be58a7c14ba"}],"id":"b835e933-57e6-472c-9274-361e629d01b2","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92572047-04a5-47e6-987f-f20b31e0f66f","uuid":"990d67f6-058f-4a1d-a2a5-08da21ac606c","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:29:16.038Z","thinking_duration_ms":28343}
