{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the full schema. The key branch (the one with transition) says:\n\n```\nExpected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched:\n  Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched:\n    Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\n    Multiple issues at [0].action.transition:\n      Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' at [0].action.transition.type\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.direction\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.matchLayers\n      Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\n  Expected null, received object at [0].action.transition\n```\n\nWait, this branch appears WITHIN one of the action variants — but which type did that branch expect? The message order: branches are CONDITIONAL, BACK|CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME ×3, then this transition branch, then SET_VARIABLE... The transition branch didn't complain about action.type or destinationId or navigation! So the branch that accepts destinationId+navigation has these transition requirements:\n\nTransition options in that branch:\n1. `{type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration, easing: {...}}` — the first sub-branch says \"Required value missing at transition.easing\" (only missing easing!) — so DISSOLVE IS valid but requires `easing`. Wait, first sub-branch: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched: Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing\" — this is a nested oneOf where one variant only complained about missing easing, meaning that variant accepted type DISSOLVE + duration but required easing. Hmm, but DISSOLVE in Figma API normally has optional easing. Here it's required.\n\nActually wait — looking again: the nested oneOf has 2 variants:\n- Variant 1: transition with type... it complained \"Required value missing at transition.easing\" ONLY. So variant 1 = {type: DISSOLVE?, duration?, easing required}. Hmm, but then variant 2: \"Multiple issues: Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE'... Required: direction, matchLayers, easing\" — that's the directional transition variant (MOVE_IN etc. need direction, matchLayers, easing).\n- Variant 2 of outer: \"Expected null, received object at transition\" — a variant where transition must be null.\n\nHmm, so where's SMART_ANIMATE/DISSOLVE? This SDK's transition schema seems limited: it seems the accepted transition types are only directional ones (MOVE_IN, MOVE_OUT, PUSH, SLIDE_IN, SLIDE_OUT) plus maybe DISSOLVE with easing. The first sub-branch accepted DISSOLVE but demanded easing. So:\n\n`transition: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing: <Easing>}`\n\nWhat Easing shapes? Figma API Easing: `{type: \"EASE_IN\"|\"EASE_OUT\"|\"EASE_IN_OUT\"|\"LINEAR\"|\"EASE_IN_BACK\"|\"EASE_OUT_BACK\"|\"EASE_IN_OUT_BACK\"|\"BOUNCY\"|\"GENTLE\"|\"QUICK\"|\"BEZIER\", ...}`. For BEZIER: {type:\"BEZIER\", easingFunction...}? Actually plugin API Easing = {type:\"BEZIER\", easingFunctionMirroring?: ...} hmm. Simplest: {type:\"LINEAR\"} or {type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"}. Let me try `{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"}}`. Hmm wait — does duration belong? First sub-branch complained ONLY about easing, so duration was accepted. \n\nBut hold on — which action branch was this? The outer branch containing the transition check must be the NODE action branch. It didn't complain about `type: \"NODE\"`, `destinationId`, or `navigation` — those were accepted there. But wait, why did branch list show this transition error at the position after UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME ×3? Because zod evaluates branches in order; this branch's ONLY issue was the transition. So the correct full shape:\n\n`{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_IN_OUT\"}}}}`\n\nAlso possibly `navigation` accepts \"NAVIGATE\" | \"OVERLAY\" | \"CHANGE_TO\" | \"SWAP\". The branch didn't flag navigation, so \"NAVIGATE\" was accepted. \n\nAlso trigger: accepted ({type:\"ON_CLICK\"} no complaints).\n\nLet me test this final shape, plus alternatives for easing ({type:\"LINEAR\"}, {type:\"BEZIER\", ...}) if needed. Also test overlay action for the cart drawer: navigation:\"OVERLAY\" might need additional fields (overlay: {type:\"POSITIONED\"...}? In plugin API, overlay for OVERLAY navigation is optional `overlay?: Overlay {type:\"POSITIONED\"|\"MANUAL\", ...}`). Let me test both NAVIGATE and OVERLAY.\n\nAlso test \"CHANGE_TO\" for the Leviosa hover? No — hover card will just be a separate frame state (04 over 03 as separate frames). Not needed.\n\nTest now:\n1. NODE/NAVIGATE + DISSOLVE+EASE_IN_OUT\n2. NODE/NAVIGATE + DISSOLVE+LINEAR\n3. NODE/OVERLAY + DISSOLVE (drawer open) — maybe needs overlay object\n4. BACK action: {type:\"BACK\"} probably works\n5. Also test trigger ON_HOVER? Not needed.\n\nIf easing variants fail, try {type:\"BEZIER\", easingFunction:{...}}? Hard to guess. EASE_IN_OUT most likely fine.\n\nLet me also plan: after confirming, I'll build frames. This test call is quick.","signature":"bc2a5467bf0f499a8decb22a"}],"id":"7f4c0d49-65f7-412e-847f-b03f3848a761","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92572047-04a5-47e6-987f-f20b31e0f66f","uuid":"f9c97a21-1eb4-4f39-b93f-9765976688f2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:29:59.736Z","thinking_duration_ms":26374}
