wait INSIDE: `await ph.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(data[6]))`. After this, `ph` might be DETACHED because swapComponent... no, swap keeps the node.\n\nLet me just test directly: create one instance of 20:39, dump its full subtree with names/types. That's the reliable way. Small diagnostic call.\n\nAlso possible: in the failed FIRST attempt of frame 01 build, the error at ph.x=0 occurred AFTER g1.appendChild? No — cardInst(PRODS[0]) threw at ph.x=0 before returning, so inst was orphaned. Whatever.\n\nBut here's another thought: in THIS second call, the error might occur on a later product (PRODS[3] Respira?) — no wait, all with badges: PRODS[0] Syltherine(-30%), PRODS[2] Lolito(-50%), PRODS[3] Respira(New). If PRODS[0] succeeded (swap+resize+texts+badge visible), then PRODS[2]... all same. Hmm.\n\nDiagnostic: dump subtree of instance. Do it.","signature":"641bd860dc1c499bb3c4791d"}],"id":"5d1fc02a-c8ed-48f5-bf0b-43239fb07226","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92572047-04a5-47e6-987f-f20b31e0f66f","uuid":"2851b001-5fd9-4a40-97b2-8f776d36bbc8","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:36:58.181Z","thinking_duration_ms":37210}
