he badge was never created in the master?! But the masters call succeeded... UNLESS the master PC 20:39 was created in the FIRST masters call attempt that partially failed? No — the masters call was a single successful call (returned FS/PB/PC/PH/PG/BP ids).\n\nHmm wait, let me re-read the masters call code for badge:\n\n```js\nconst pw = frame(\"PhotoWrap\",300,280,PC); pw.fills=[hex(\"F4F3EF\")]; pw.clipsContent=true;\nconst ph = await comp(\"13:21\"); ph.resize(300,280); ph.name=\"Photo\"; pw.appendChild(ph); ph.x=0; ph.y=0;\nconst badge = frame(\"Badge\",48,48,pw); badge.x=236; badge.y=16; badge.cornerRadius=8; badge.fills=[hex(\"E97132\")]; badge.visible=false;\nconst bt = txt(\"-30%\",\"SemiBold\",14,\"FFFFFF\"); bt.name=\"BadgeLabel\"; badge.appendChild(bt); bt.x=(48-bt.width)/2; bt.y=(48-bt.height)/2;\n```\n\nHmm — badge.visible=false... then later `out.PC_h=PC.height` = 434.\n\nWait, actually — I wonder if the dump was truncated? dump depth limit d<4: INSTANCE(0) > PhotoWrap(1) > children(2). Badge would show at depth 2. Not truncation.\n\nAlternatively — setting `badge.visible=false` on a FRAME inside a COMPONENT... when the component has an invisible child, and you create an INSTANCE, invisible children ARE included... I'm fairly sure they are. But the dump directly shows the master's structure mirrored — Photo only.\n\nLet me check the MASTER directly (20:39) — dump its subtree. If Badge missing in master → masters call bug. Actually — OH WAIT. I see it!!! In the masters call, look at the line:\n\n`const bt = txt(\"-30%\",\"SemiBold\",14,\"FFFFFF\"); bt.name=\"BadgeLabel\"; badge.appendChild(bt); bt.x=(48-bt.width)/2; bt.y=(48-bt.height)/2;`\n\nNo issue there. Hmm.\n\nBut hold on — maybe the issue is `badge.visible=false` BEFORE appendChild of bt... no, badge already appended to pw at creation.\n\nActually, wait — maybe the issue is different: `frame(\"Badge\",48,48,pw)` — frame() sets name, resize, appendChild. Then `badge.x=236` — pw is NOT auto-layout 