{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Badge EXISTS in the master (vis=false) but is absent from the instance subtree. So confirmed: Figma plugin API does NOT include invisible main-component children in the instance's subtree (children/findAll/findOne). That's the known behavior — hidden nodes are not instantiated unless... hmm, actually instances DO render hidden layers when you toggle them via override, but the API subtree for instances apparently only contains nodes that are visible? Interesting quirk of this environment.\n\nSolution: make Badge VISIBLE in the master (visible=true), and hide it per-instance via override... but if invisible nodes don't exist in instances, setting instance override `bd.visible=false` on an instance whose master node is visible — the node EXISTS in instance (visible in master) so findOne finds it, and setting visible=false as an override should work.\n\nSo: update master: Badge.visible = true. Then in cardInst: badge default — instances inherit visible=true → badges would show on ALL cards by default. In cardInst, for cards WITHOUT badge, set bd.visible=false (override). For cards WITH badge, set fills + label.\n\nBut wait — does setting visible=false on an instance child work as an override? Yes, visibility overrides are standard.\n\nAlso same consideration for future: any master content that must be hidden by default and shown per-instance → keep visible in master, override-hide in instances.\n\nAlso, important for the master's own appearance on the page: master Badge will now be visible showing \"-30%\" — that's fine (it's a component spec sheet, though the badge shows on master — acceptable; masters section is documentation).\n\nAlternatively invert: Badge visible in master; cardInst hides when data[4] is null.\n\nUpdate the masters: set 20:39 Badge.visible = true. Then rebuild 01_Home (the partial from last call? The second 01_Home call failed at cardInst — but it had already removed old 01_Home and created header/hero/range/partial products... The call failed mid-way; partial frame exists again. My rebuild code removes existing \"01_Home\" first, so fine.\n\nAlso fix cardInst: \n```js\nasync function cardInst(data){\n  const inst=...createInstance();\n  const ph=inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Photo\");\n  await ph.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(data[6]));\n  ph.resize(300,280);\n  ... texts ...\n  const bd=inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Badge\");\n  if (data[4]){ bd.fills=[hex(data[5])]; inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"BadgeLabel\").characters=data[4]; }\n  else bd.visible=false;\n  return inst;\n}\n```\nNote: swap before or after badge handling? Badge is sibling of Photo — swap doesn't affect it (confirmed findAll count 0 was pre-swap issue; post-swap also 0 because invisible). With Badge visible in master, it will be in instance from creation.\n\nOne more check — after swapComponent, does the instance re-render and REMOVE badge override? Badge isn't affected by photo swap. OK.\n\nAlso the earlier x/y error: don't set ph.x/ph.y on nested instance. After swap, ph position: swapComponent preserves position? The swap test earlier suggested resize OK. Position may reset to new component's origin? Photo components have various sizes; when swapped, the instance node keeps its x/y (node properties persist except fills/components). Actually swapComponent docs: \"Swaps out a nested instance's component while preserving overrides where possible\" — position should persist. I'll trust and verify visually.\n\nAlso — Label naming: master Photo instance resized 300×280 in master. After swap to a component of e.g. 295×240, the instance SIZE stays 300×280 (node size preserved), just new content. Actually then ph.resize is redundant but harmless. But x/y — node position preserved. Good.\n\nCombine: Call now = (1) set master Badge visible, (2) rebuild 01_Home fully. Also should double check the partial 01_Home from the last failed call gets removed (my code does that).\n\nLet me also make sure the failed second call didn't leave orphan product card instances floating on the page (created inside g1 before failing — they were children of g1 which is child of ps → child of F \"01_Home\" — all removed with F). But ALSO: cardInst created `inst` and appended to g1 — fine, removed with F. However in the FIRST failed 01 call, cardInst errored at ph.x=0 BEFORE appendChild — that inst was floating at (0,0)? In first call: `g1.appendChild(await cardInst(PRODS[0]))` — cardInst threw before returning, so inst never appended — orphan at root of page (0,0)?? figma.createInstance() without append — it goes to currentPage. In the plugin API, createInstance appends to figma.currentPage by default! So orphan instances may be floating on page 15:2 at 0,0. In the second call error: bd.visible threw after inst was appended to g1 (g1.appendChild(await cardInst(...)) — the await completed? No! cardInst threw DURING execution, so the appendChild never ran; inst orphaned on page).\n\nSo clean up: remove any floating INSTANCE nodes named \"Product Card\"/\"Product Card Hover\" that are direct children of ws (my masters are COMPONENT type, instances created were INSTANCE). Also any orphan \"Header\"/\"Footer\" instances. I'll add cleanup: for ch of [...ws.children] remove if ch.type===\"INSTANCE\" (direct page children shouldn't be instances — all instances live inside frames) — safe. Also remove stray TEXT/FRAME orphans? Only remove instances to be safe, plus frames named \"01_Home\" (rebuild removes).\n\nWrite the combined call now.","signature":"08149b99be224d82bb72ab46"}],"id":"30009b5d-96ef-44ce-83ee-533736ed3757","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92572047-04a5-47e6-987f-f20b31e0f66f","uuid":"62e65cbf-4e34-4abf-b620-e5c4d0de96e2","timestamp":"2026-11-01T19:38:25.085Z","thinking_d