{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark: build the complete \"Furniro — furniture store website\" (desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode) inside page \"03 · Workspace\" (node **15:2**) of the assigned file https://www.figma.com/design/iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG/ (fileKey `iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG`). Requirements:\n   - Account confirmed: zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (verified via whoami earlier; \"Sensenova design\" plan, Full seat).\n   - Follow \"00 · Start Here\" brief exactly; use \"01 · Foundations\" rules (brand #B88E2F + Poppins FIXED; all else designer-defined consistently); reuse \"02 · Components\" (Button 1:23, Text Field 1:26) and \"04 · Media\" assets.\n   - Build exactly 9 frames named exactly: 01_Home, 02_Shop, 03_Product, 04_Cart_Drawer, 05_Comparison, 06_Cart, 07_Checkout, 08_Contact, 09_Blog (one state per frame), wired as clickable prototype with the listed links. Copy/data verbatim from \"Fixed data\". Header, footer, navigation and every business component as reusable components. Frame names fixed; must-include lists state WHAT not layout.\n   - Preserve all reference pages (00/01/02/04) and their nodes; keep unrelated content intact; do NOT create a different file or switch accounts.\n   - Before EVERY tool call include a visible decision summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:`; after each tool result do the same; final response starts with `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:` with the assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n   - Inspect screenshots of all screens, fix visible problems, finish screens/states/prototype flows before final answer. Unattended session — resolve routine choices using the brief.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - `mcp__figma__use_figma` JS execution (50k char limit, no persistent state — helpers redefined every call; failed calls leave partial state, NO rollback — cleanup pattern: remove same-named frame + stray INSTANCE children before rebuild)\n   - **STALE-HEIGHT TRAP (root cause of 03/05 failures)**: reading `.height` immediately after setting layoutMode or on a freshly-hugging frame can return stale values (e.g. createFrame default 100 or 0); `resize()` sets BOTH axes to FIXED simultaneously. Safe pattern for full-width sections: `f.resize(1440, 10)` (constant, no read) THEN explicitly restore the hug axis: HORIZONTAL rows → `f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"; f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"`; VERTICAL sections → `f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"; f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"`.\n   - **Font loading required before ANY text property write** (characters, textAutoResize, etc.): `await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:\"Regular\"})` etc. before touching text nodes.\n   - **Plain frames do NOT flow children** — children default to (0,0); must either use auto-layout or set x/y manually (04 drawer bug).\n   - **VERTICAL auto-layout: primary axis = height.** Setting primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\" on a VERTICAL container clips vertically (04 items bug hiding Subtotal row).\n   - **Prototype wiring (CONFIRMED WORKING)**: `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:\"ON_CLICK\"}, actions:[{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:\"<frameId>\", navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:{type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"LINEAR\"}}}]}]` — plural `actions` array INSIDE the reaction object REQUIRED; easing MUST be `{type:\"LINEAR\"}`; BACK = `{actions:[{type:\"BACK\"}]}`.\n   - Invisible master nodes are ABSENT from instance subtrees (master 20:39 Badge visible=true; hide via override).\n   - Nested instance: cannot set x/y; `resize()` and `swapComponent()` work.\n   - Poppins styles: \"SemiBold\" (no space), \"Bold\", \"Medium\", \"Regular\".\n   - get_screenshot returns URL+curl or base64 (enableBase64Response:true); maxDimension caps longer edge; one 120s timeout occurred — simple retry works.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG** — pages: 0:1 \"00 · Start Here\", 1:2 \"01 · Foundations\", 1:3 \"02 · Components\", 1:4 \"04 · Media\", 15:2 \"03 · Workspace\" (build target).\n   - **Built frames so far (all on 15:2)**:\n     - 01_Home **28:2** (x=0,y=0, h=5177) — verified GOOD (header Nav_Home gold, hero, BrowseRange, 8 product cards w/ Leviosa hover, ShowMore, Inspiration slider, ShareSetup 2 rows, footer).\n     - 02_Shop **29:2** (x=1600,y=0, h=3298) — verified GOOD (header Nav_Shop gold, banner Title/CrumbPage=\"Shop\", toolbar, 16 cards rows seq [0-7,0-7] w/ hover 20:50 at r0c1, pagination 20:75, strip 20:4, footer 19:22).\n     - 03_Product **31:2** (x=0,y=5400, h=2545) — verified GOOD (header Shop gold; breadcrumb Home›Shop›Asgaard sofa ids 31:25/31:26/31:29/31:32; Main 31:33 with Gallery 31:34 [MainPhoto 31:35=13:4 550×530, Thumbs 31:37: 13:14/13:15/13:64/13:13 107×107] + Summary 31:46 [title, Rs. 250,000.00 #B0B0B0, 4 stars 13:31+half 13:52 #FFC700 + \"204 Customer Reviews\", short desc, Size L(selected #B88E2F)/XL/XS 36×36, colors purple #816DFA ring/black/gold 30px, Qty 140×56 −1+, AddToCart 1:23 inst 178×56 \"+...\" wait \"Add To Cart\", \"+ Compare\" outline 150×56, SKU SS001/Category Sofas/Tags Sofa, Chair, Home, Shop, Share + 13:44/13:35/13:36]; DescriptionSection 31:107 [Tabs 31:108 layoutMode=NONE texts Description SemiBold 20 dark/Additional Information/Reviews [204] + Underline 31:112 x=0 y=30 w=117; DescBody: DescText 640 wide ¶1+¶2 + Cloud1 13:7 & Cloud2 13:8 312×300]; Related 31:122 [Syltherine/Leviosa/Lolito/Respira cards + ShowMore 245×56 outline]; footer).\n     - 04_Cart_Drawer **34:2** (x=1600,y=3600, 1440×1080 fixed) — verified GOOD (backdrop: header 19:4 Shop gold, absolute breadcrumb texts at y=126 + carets 13:46, MainPhoto 13:4 at (54,180) 550×530, title (669,200), price (669,266); Scrim 1440×1080 hex(\"24252B\",0.4); CartDrawer **34:37** 480×1080 at x=960 white + drop shadow (-8,0,24,0.25): DrawerHeader (Shopping Cart SemiBold 24 + Icon_Cart_Close 13:39 26px) y=0 h=92; Items y=100 (Item: photo 13:4 100×100 + \"Asgaard sofa\" Medium 16 + \"1 × Rs. 250,000.00\" Regular 14 #898989 + remove Icon_Remove 13:43; SubtotalRow SPACE_BETWEEN \"Subtotal\" + \"Rs. 250,000.00\" gold, h=28); DrawerDiv 416×1 #D9D9D9 y=304; DrawerButtons y=329: Cart outline 100w, Checkout filled #B88E2F 120w, Comparison outline 140w, all 48h white/brand text Medium 14).\n     - 05_Comparison **37:2** (x=1600,y=4900, h=3014 after fix, NOT yet re-screenshotted) — header 19:4 (no current), banner Title=\"Product Comparison\"/CrumbPage=\"Comparison\", Intro row (SPACE_BETWEEN: left \"Add A Product\" gray + row [\"Go to Product page for more Products\" SemiBold 24 + ViewMore outline 168×48]; right \"Add A Product\" + Select 370×56 \"Choose a Product\" + chevron 13:30), ProdHead (spacer 290 + PCol 13:4 \"Asgaard Sofa\" Rs. 250,000.00 star \"4.7\" \"204 Review\" | PCol 13:14 \"Outdoor Sofa Set\" Rs. 224,000.00 \"4.2\" \"145 Review\"; photo 170×130, star 13:31 #FFC700), ATCRow (spacer 290 + 2 outline \"Add To Cart\" 180×56 brand), SpecTable (group headers SemiBold 20 + 22 rows: label text fixed w=290 Regular 16 #898989, V1/V2 frames 490 wide with value Regular 14 #3A3A3A lh20 w470, rows strokeBottomWeight=1 #E5E5E5; groups General 6/Product 5/Dimensions 6/Warranty 5 with verbatim values: Sales Package \"1 sectional sofa\"|\"1 Three Seater, 2 Single Seater\"; Model TFCBLIGRBL6SRHS|DTUBLIGRBL568; Solid Wood×2; L-shaped; Fabric + Cotton; Bright Grey & Lion; Foam; Matte; No|Yes; 280 KG|300 KG; India; 265.32 cm; 76 cm; 167.76 cm; 45 KG|65 KG; 41.52 cm; 5.46 cm; \"1 Year Manufacturing Warranty\"|\"1.2 Year Manufacturing Warranty\"; operations@furniro.example|support@furniro.example warranty service; \"Warranty Against Manufacturing Defect\"|\"Warranty of the product is limited to manufacturing defects only.\"; Not Covered same text both; \"1 Year\"|\"3 Months\"), strip 20:4, footer 19:22).\n   - **Component masters (on 15:2)**: Header **19:4** (texts Nav_Home/Nav_Shop/Nav_About/Nav_Contact; Icon_Account 13:33/Icon_Search 13:40/Icon_Heart 13:53/Icon_Cart 13:26); Footer **19:22** (Link_Home/Link_Shop/Link_About/Link_Contact/Link_Blog); FeatureStrip **20:4**; PageBanner **20:29** (override Title/CrumbPage; CrumbHome + chevron 13:46 + CrumbPage); Product Card **20:39** (Photo/Badge+BadgeLabel/Name/Description/Price/OldPrice); Product Card Hover **20:50** (Leviosa + overlay AddToCart/Share/Compare/Like); Pagination **20:75**; Blog Post Card **20:84** (Photo/Meta/Title/Excerpt/ReadMore); Button **1:23** (single TEXT child); Text Field **1:26**.\n   - **Helper functions (redefine EVERY call — current canonical versions)**:\n```js\nfor (const s of [\"Regular\",\"Medium\",\"SemiBold\",\"Bold\"]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:\"Poppins\",style:s});\nfunction hex(h,o){const n=parseInt(h,16);return {type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o===undefined?1:o};}\nfunction txt(chars,style,size,colorHex,opts={}){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:\"Poppins\",style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[hex(colorHex)];if(opts.ls!==undefined)t.letterSpacing={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:opts.ls};if(opts.lh)t.lineHeight={unit:\"PIXELS\",value:opts.lh};if(opts.deco)t.textDecoration=opts.deco;if(opts.w){t.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\";t.resize(opts.w,t.height);}if(opts.align)t.textAlignHorizontal=opts.align;return t;}\nfunction autolayout(name,dir,gap,pT,pR,pB,pL,parent){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.layoutMode=dir;f.itemSpacing=gap;f.paddingTop=pT;f.paddingRight=pR;f.paddingBottom=pB;f.paddingLeft=pL;f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";f.fills=[];if(parent)parent.appendChild(f);return f;}\nfunction fullRow(f,primaryFixed){f.resize(1440,10);if(primaryFixed){f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";}else{f.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\";f.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\";}} // CORRECTED VERSION - must restore both axes\nfunction frame(name,w,h,parent,x,y){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;if(w)f.resize(w,h);if(parent)parent.appendChild(f);if(x!==undefined)f.x=x;if(y!==undefined)f.y=y;return f;}\nasync function comp(id){return (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)).createInstance();}\nasync function icon(id,size,colorHex,parent,name){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);const i=c.createInstance();i.resize(size,size*(c.height/c.width));i.name=name;if(colorHex){for(const d of i.findAll(n=>[\"VECTOR\",\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\",\"TEXT\",\"RECTANGLE\"].includes(n.type))){if(\"fills\" in d){try{d.fills=[hex(colorHex)];}catch(e){}}}}if(parent)parent.appendChild(i);return i;}\nasync function photoFrame(parent,name,w,h,x,y,r,photoId){const f=frame(name,w,h,parent,x,y);f.fills=[hex(\"F4F3EF\")];f.clipsContent=true;if(r)f.cornerRadius=r;const p=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(photoId)).createInstance();f.appendChild(p);p.resize(w,h);return f;}\nconst PRODS = [[\"Syltherine\",\"Stylish cafe chair\",\"Rs. 2,500,000.00\",\"Rs. 3,500,000.00\",\"-30%\",\"E97132\",\"13:21\"],[\"Leviosa\",\"Stylish cafe chair\",\"Rs. 2,500,000.00\",null,null,null,\"13:17\"],[\"Lolito\",\"Luxury big sofa\",\"Rs. 7,000,000.00\",\"Rs. 14,000,000.00\",\"-50%\",\"E97132\",\"13:18\"],[\"Respira\",\"Outdoor bar table and stool\",\"Rs. 500,000.00\",null,\"New\",\"2EC1AC\",\"13:20\"],[\"Grifo\",\"Night lamp\",\"Rs. 1,500,000.00\",null,null,null,\"13:73\"],[\"Muggo\",\"Small mug\",\"Rs. 150,000.00\",null,\"New\",\"2EC1AC\",\"13:19\"],[\"Pingky\",\"Cute bed set\",\"Rs. 7,000,000.00\",\"Rs. 14,000,000.00\",\"-50%\",\"E97132\",\"13:67\"],[\"Potty\",\"Minimalist flower pot\",\"Rs. 500,000.00\",null,\"New\",\"2EC1AC\",\"13:66\"]];\nasync function cardInst(data){const inst=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"20:39\")).createInstance();const ph=inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Photo\");await ph.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(data[6]));ph.resize(300,280);inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Name\").characters=data[0];inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Description\").characters=data[1];inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Price\").characters=data[2];inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"OldPrice\").characters=data[3]||\"\";const bd=inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"Badge\");if(data[4]){bd.fills=[hex(data[5])];inst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"BadgeLabel\").characters=data[4];}else{bd.visible=false;}return inst;}\n```\n   Page frame creation pattern: `F.layoutMode=\"VERTICAL\"; F.itemSpacing=0; F.resize(1440,1000); F.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"; F.counterAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"; F.fills=[hex(\"FFFFFF\")];`\n   - **Design system**: brand #B88E2F; cream #FBF1E7; card photo bg #F4F3EF; dark #24252B; body #3A3A3A; gray #898989; light #B0B0B0; border #E5E5E5; input border #9F9F9F; sale #E97132; new #2EC1AC; footer bg #1F1F24; star #FFC700. Primary btn brand bg white text; secondary white bg 1px brand border brand text.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **03_Product tab() crash**: `tabs.getItem(...)` — \"no such property 'getItem' on FRAME node\". Fixed by rebuilding; underline appended to tabs auto-layout then repositioned. Residual: underline pushed to end of auto-layout row → fixed later by `tabs.layoutMode=\"NONE\"` + `ul.x=0; ul.y=30`.\n   - **Stale-height resize bug (03_Product)**: `bc.resize(1440,bc.height)` right after creating/adding children captured height 100 (unflushed layout), setting counterAxis FIXED at 100 → Main (h=100) clipped its 699px content (Summary showed only title, MainPhoto appeared as empty gray slice). Fixed: resize then explicit sizing modes (Main/Breadcrumb: primary FIXED + counter AUTO; DescriptionSection/Related: counter FIXED + primary AUTO). Result h 1906→2545, verified GOOD.\n   - **04 drawer children stacked at (0,0)**: dr was a plain frame, auto-layout children never given y. Fix attempt 1 failed: guessed id \"34:33\" → \"cannot set property 'x' of undefined\"; found CartDrawer by name (34:37) and set dh.y=0, items.y=100, dv.y=224, btns.y=249.\n   - **04 Subtotal row invisible**: items is VERTICAL auto-layout and I had set `items.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"FIXED\"` (primary=height) clipping at 100. Fix: `items.primaryAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"`; repositioned dv.y=304, btns.y=329; `sub.resize(416,28)`. Verified GOOD.\n   - **05 fullRow bug**: `f.resize(1440,10)` sets BOTH axes FIXED; fullRow(true) only restored primary → all H rows fixed at 10px height, content clipped/overlapping (Intro/ProdHead/ATCRow/spec rows). Fix: set `counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\"` on all those rows (h 2054→3014, intro 160, ph 162, atc 96).\n   - **05 column misalignment**: spec row labels were hug-width so V1/V2 value frames started at varying x. Fix: for all 22 rows, `lab.textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\"; lab.resize(290,lab.height)` (label col fixed 290 aligning with 290 spacers in ProdHead/ATCRow; V1/V2 frames are 490 wide).\n   - **Font unload error in fix call**: setting `textAutoResize` without loaded font → \"Cannot write to node with unloaded font 'Poppins Regular'\". Fix: always `await figma.loadFontAsync(...)` at top of every call that touches text.\n   - One get_screenshot 120s timeout on 31:2 — simple retry succeeded.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Systematic diagnosis via read-only tree dumps (dump children with name/type/id/w/h) to find clipped-content root causes rather than guessing.\n   - Established the deterministic fullRow pattern (resize with constant, then restore both sizing modes explicitly) to avoid the stale-height trap in remaining frames.\n   - 04_Cart_Drawer solved via manual y-positioning inside a plain-frame drawer (backdrop composition: real header instance + absolute breadcrumb + scrim + overlay drawer).\n   - 05_Comparison data fully entered verbatim (4 spec groups, 22 rows); fix applied and metrics confirm heights hug correctly (intro=160, ph=162, atc=96, 22 labels fixed) — pending visual confirmation.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Original request, prior sessions, in Chinese): “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。”\n   - (This session) Only the continuation system message instructing to resume from the summary without acknowledging it; no new human-authored messages. Standing benchmark constraints: use only the assigned file; account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai confirmed; preserve reference pages (00/01/02/04) and unrelated content; deliver in 03 · Workspace (15:2); report file URL, page ID, screen IDs, prototype work, limitations; `Reasoning summary:` before every tool call and after every tool result; `Final answer:` in the final response; never claim completion for unfinished work.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Screenshot-verify 05_Comparison (37:2) after the row-height/column fix.\n   - Build 06_Cart (x=1600, y≈8100 — below 05 which ends ~7914; keep ~30px gaps): header 19:4 (NO nav highlighted), banner Title=\"Cart\"/CrumbPage=\"Cart\", cart table (header row Product|Price|Quantity|Subtotal; row: photo 13:4 ~100×100 + \"Asgaard sofa\" | Rs. 250,000.00 | \"1\" | Rs. 250,000.00 + Icon_Delete 13:28), Cart Totals card (title SemiBold 24; Subtotal row; Total row bolder; Check Out primary brand button), FeatureStrip 20:4, footer 19:22. LINKS: Check Out→07, \"Asgaard sofa\" name→03, breadcrumb Home→01.\n   - Build 08_Contact (x=1600 after 06): header (Nav_Contact gold), banner \"Contact\"/CrumbPage=\"Contact\", \"Get In Touch With Us\" SemiBold ~36 + intro \"For more information about our products & services, please feel free to drop us an email. Our staff will always be there to help you out. Do not hesitate!\", 3 info cards (Icon_Location 13:29/Address/\"236 5th SE Avenue, New York NY10000, United States\"; Icon_Phone 13:32/Phone/\"Mobile: +(84) 546-6789\" + \"Hotline: +(84) 456-6789\"; Icon_Clock 13:54/Working Time/\"Monday–Friday: 9:00 – 22:00\" + \"Saturday–Sunday: 9:00 – 21:00\"), form (Text Field 1:26 instances: Your name \"Abc\", Email address \"Abc@def.com\", Subject \"This is optional\", Message \"Hi! I'd like to ask about\" taller, Submit Button 1:23), strip+footer. LINK: Home→01.\n   - Build 07_Checkout (x=0 below 05, y≈8100-8200): header (no current), banner \"Checkout\"/Home›Checkout, left Billing details with Text Field 1:26 instances (First Name, Last Name, Company Name (Optional), Country / Region→\"Sri Lanka\"+Icon_Chevron_Down 13:30, Street address, Town / City, Province→\"Western Province\"+chevron, ZIP code, Phone, Email address, Additional information), Payment section (radio selected Direct Bank Transfer + note \"Make your payment directly into our bank account. Please use your Order ID as the payment reference. Your order will not be shipped until the funds have cleared in our account.\"; radio Cash On Delivery), privacy note \"Your personal data will be used to support your experience throughout this website, to manage access to your account, and for other purposes described in our privacy policy.\" with underlined \"privacy policy\" + \"Place order\" Button 1:23 primary; right order summary card (headers Product|Subtotal; \"Asgaard sofa ×  1\" Rs. 250,000.00; Subtotal Rs. 250,000.00; Total Rs. 250,000.00), strip+footer. Place order = entry only.\n   - Build 09_Blog (x=0 below 07): header (no current), banner \"Blog\"/Home›Blog, 3 BlogPostCard 20:84 instances (Photo swap 13:5/13:68/13:6, Category Wood/Handmade/Wood, Titles \"Going all-in with millennial design\"/\"Exploring new ways of decorating\"/\"Handmade pieces that took time to make\", Admin+14 Oct 2022+Icon_User 13:45/Icon_Calendar 13:37/Icon_Tag 13:27, exact excerpts from brief, Read more), sidebar ~340 (search box Icon_Search 13:40; Categories Crafts 2·Design 8·Handmade 7·Interior 1·Wood 6; Recent Posts 5 rows thumb ~70×70 photos 13:65/13:71/13:55/13:56/13:57 + titles + 03 Aug 2022), Pagination 20:75, strip+footer. LINK: Home→01.\n   - Wire ALL prototype links (confirmed reactions format): masters — ProductCard 20:39 root→28:2? NO: 20:39→03 frame 31:2; Hover 20:50 Compare action→05 (37:2); Header 19:4: Nav_Home→28:2, Nav_Shop→29:2, Nav_Contact→08 frame, Icon_Cart→06 frame; Footer 19:22: Link_Home→28:2, Link_Blog→09 frame; PageBanner 20:29 CrumbHome→28:2. Frame-specific — 01 (28:2): BUY NOW→29:2, ShowMore→29:2; 03 (31:2): AddToCart btn→34:2, +Compare→37:2, Shop crumb 31:29→29:2; 04 (34:2): BtnCart→06, BtnCheckout→07, BtnComparison→37:2, close icon→31:2 (or BACK); 05 (37:2): ViewMore→29:2, ATC1+ATC2→06; 06: CheckOut→07, \"Asgaard sofa\"→31:2; 07: Place order entry-only; 08: Home→28:2; 09: Home→28:2. Entry-only (no link): About, account, search, wishlist, Explore More, slide arrows, range tiles, Add to cart/Share/Like on cards, Filter, view toggles, Show, Sort by, pagination, size, color, quantity, social share, description tabs, Choose a Product, all form fields, Submit, Subscribe, Read more, categories, recent posts.\n   - Screenshot-verify all remaining frames (06/07/08/09 + re-verify 05), fix visible problems, re-verify.\n   - Final answer with: file URL https://www.figma.com/design/iREO0ZncSJq5Rg5HF95nYG/, workspace page ID 15:2, all 9 screen IDs (28:2, 29:2, 31:2, 34:2, 37:2, + 4 TBD), prototype work summary, remaining limitations.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just finished fixing 05_Comparison (37:2) rendering bugs. The fix call (after adding the missing font load) returned `{\"h\":3014,\"intro\":160,\"ph\":162,\"atc\":96,\"fixed\":22}` — Intro/ProdHead/ATCRow heights now hug correctly and all 22 spec-row labels are fixed at width 290 for column alignment. The fix has NOT yet been visually verified with a screenshot. Immediately before this, 05's first screenshot had shown collapsed rows (Intro/ProdHead content clipped, spec rows squished at 10px with overlapping text) caused by fullRow(true) not restoring counterAxisSizingMode=\"AUTO\" after resize() fixed both axes, plus hug-width labels misaligning value columns. All four previously built frames (01_Home 28:2, 02_Shop 29:2, 03_Product 31:2, 04_Cart_Drawer 34:2) are screenshot-verified GOOD.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Screenshot-verify the fixed 05_Comparison (get_screenshot nodeId 37:2, enableBase64Response true, maxDimension ~1500) to confirm Intro row (bold text + View More + Choose a Product select), product comparison columns (photos/names/prices/ratings), and all 22 spec rows render cleanly with aligned columns. If good, proceed to build 06_Cart next per the plan (\"Build 06_Cart (x=1600, y≈8100): header (no current), banner 'Cart', cart table..., Cart Totals card..., FeatureStrip, footer\"), continuing through 07_Checkout, 08_Contact, 09_Blog, then wire all prototype links with the confirmed reactions format, then final verification screenshots of all remaining screens.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/web10-main-v4-20261102/runs/TEST-031_1793560335630/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-web10-main-v4-20261102-workspace/92572047-04a5-47e6-987f-f20b31e0f66f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92